{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/646604-resources-and-possessions-of-enemies","id":646604,"title":"Resources and possessions of enemies.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-08-31T06:41:04-07:00","id":646604,"title":"Resources and possessions of enemies.","content":"I am getting ready to start running a full cWoD Main characters are Vampires. I am planning ahead and wanted to find out what others do.<br /> <br /> An example, The characters have just finished killing a Vampire that has caused a breach of the Masquerade. This vampire had a resources of 4, had a collection of guns and bodyguards that they had to disable.<br /> <br /> So the group is wanting to assume ownership of the cars and weapons. One of them is a gunsmith and owns a gun shop. Others in the group are computer hackers and B&amp;E people.<br /> <br /> How would you handle this?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7535-chaifi","name":"Chaifi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7535_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-31T09:34:30-07:00","id":646881,"title":"","content":"Backgrounds don't cost experience. They are expected to rise and fall over the course of the game based on the results of the narrative.<br /> <br /> If it makes sense for the player characters to take over the NPC's resources and possessions, there's no reason not to. If it doesn't make sense in the situation as it stands, then it doesn't have to happen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-31T13:43:43-07:00","id":647151,"title":"","content":"Sounds like they'll need the help of someone skilled at forging title deeds and bills of sale. Which could be a fun story in and of itself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-31T15:15:13-07:00","id":647267,"title":"","content":"Yeah. Remember that someone might report those cars and weapons stolen to the police.Obviously you don't want to be a dick and punish your players needlessly, but in the modern world sometimes murdering people and taking their stuff has nasty consequences. <br /> <br /> If the player ends up selling some of the weapons down the road, it might be fun to have the police tie the gun to a crime, then tie it to the previous (now dead owner) and show up asking how the player's store got a gun from a dead person.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-01T04:59:12-07:00","id":647866,"title":"","content":"Also consider the politics of the matter. This is always a good idea with vampires.<br /> <br /> Perhaps the Prince wishes to reward the PCs for sealing up this Masquerade breach, and so will allow them to keep the loot. The Prince effectively grants them a letter of marque.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, the dead vampire may have had powerful allies or been part of a larger organization, such as being part of Clan Tremere. In this case, his belongings might be claimed by those allies or that organization, and the Prince may rule that this is correct.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />Avatar commissioned from the incomparable Melissa Uran.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/966-redford_blade","name":"Redford_Blade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar966_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-01T07:18:17-07:00","id":647963,"title":"","content":"There might well be a fence or money launderer among or connected to the local Kindred, happy to make acquisitions look legal for a fee or boon.<br /> <br /> In rules terms, if a player would like to increase their Resources I'd consider it, but the stolen goods probably aren't enough to raise anyone to as high as the destroyed vampire's Resources level as that needs an ongoing revenue stream. I'd let them keep at least some of the toys, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Craig Oxbrow<br /> <b>The Trinity Continuum</b> freelancer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/221-craig-oxbrow","name":"Craig Oxbrow","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar221_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-01T11:28:53-07:00","id":648169,"title":"","content":"Certainly as long as they're not attracting police attention waving the appropriated guns around, it's not as if authorities would know the stolen weapons are in their possession. Stolen cars are easier to spot, but fake license plates are easy to make and if you're not doing anything to attract notice they're unlikely to be run through the system.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}